title: Walk_Augustine_Bostrom
tags: walk
speaker: Augustine
---
Augustine: If I am mistaken, I exist, for one who does not exist cannot be mistaken.
Augustine: That inner certainty of existing remains firm even amidst deep sensory doubt.
Augustine: The woodland path leads on toward the grove of Probability.
Augustine: We move from inner certainty to assessing likelihoods under uncertainty.
Augustine: Notice how tall trunks block the distant sky ahead of us.
Augustine: The Academic sceptics said the wise settle for what seems probable. I argued against them.
Augustine: Nick Bostrom waits among the pines to question your expectations.
Augustine: He asks how to calculate chances when sensory proof is absent.
Augustine: Consider whether statistical odds can substitute for divine light and truth.
Augustine: Let us walk forward to hear his mathematical argument.
===
